  "description": "DGS 2026-10-03 (policy review, Academic Code §5.1 and §6.2.6), refined 2026-10-05 (policy review round 3, P3-ac-5a-1, option (a)): a leave semester is not a semester of enrollment, so a leave BEFORE the end of the eighth semester pushes the Oral Candidacy Exam and admission-to-candidacy deadline out, and every leave pushes the eight-year limit. Entered Fall 2022, on leave Fall 2024 and Spring 2025: the eighth semester of enrollment is Spring 2027 — two semesters after Spring 2026 — so on 2026-10-03 the row is still in progress and says why. (Until 2026-10-05 this fixture had the student enrolled all eight semesters and the leaves after them; such leaves no longer move the deadline — see phd-leave-after-eighth-semester.)",
